  "body": "Deadline sale: Closes on Thursday 3 December 2026 at 2:00PM  (unless sold prior)\r\n\r\nJust four luxury homes share this private Rothesay Bay address, and this one stands on its own. It’s architect-designed and carefully finished, with elevated sea views that are part of everyday life. You can walk to Rothesay Bay Beach and Reserve, and shops, buses and some of the North Shore’s most sought-after schools are all close by.\r\n\r\nInside, French-inspired design details sit alongside quality fixtures and a warm, refined feel. The layout is spread over two levels and suits families who want room to grow, or professionals who want a low-maintenance base.\r\n\r\nThe layout:\r\n• Entry level: three bedrooms and a family bathroom. This works well as a separate zone for teenagers, visiting relatives or flatmates.\r\n• Upper level: a private master retreat with a walk-in wardrobe and a beautifully appointed ensuite.\r\n• Overall: 4 bedrooms, 2.5 bathrooms, generous living areas, a single internal-access garage and gardens that need little upkeep.\r\n\r\nBuilt for year-round comfort\r\n\r\nBathrooms are fully tiled with underfloor heating. The home also has double glazing, full insulation, heat pumps and LED lighting throughout. The current owners have added solar panels and a Tesla charger, which help cut power costs and make charging an EV at home easy. It’s on a Freehold Title with no body corporate fees.\r\n\r\nThe coastal lifestyle\r\n\r\nFollow the coastal walkways to Browns Bay or Mairangi Bay village for cafés, restaurants, boutique shopping and everyday amenities. Local bus stops are nearby.\r\n\r\nIn zone for:\r\n• Browns Bay School\r\n• Murrays Bay Intermediate\r\n• Rangitoto College\r\n• Northcross Intermediate\r\n\r\nPlease call today to arrange a viewing.",
